                <pb facs="0890" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg806"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>No. 392.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gurry to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-09-30"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 30,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Curry informs Mr. Bayard that he has received the latter’s telegrams; that
                    immediate action on their subject has been promised by the minister of state. He
                    requests that the withdrawal of the proclamation of 1884 may be delayed until
                    after a definite report has been made by the legation at Madrid.</p>
            </div>
